  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A primary aliphatic amine on reaction with nitrous acid in cold gives a diazonium salt, but diazonium salt of aliphatic amines are not much stable, so, they dissociate on increasing temperature slightly and gives alcohol with water.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><munderover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><mn>273</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced></mrow></munderover><msup><msub><mi>RN</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo></msup><munderover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>283</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow></munderover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>OH</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p>",
